RFC 000: Project Master Specification & Architecture Philosophy
Status: Draft / Proposed
Project Name: OurVillage (VillageOS)
Target Stack: Pure Go, Mochi-MQTT, SQLite, RKLLM

1. Executive Summary & Vision
OurVillage is a multi-agent economic simulation and persistent, text-based environment modeled after classic village community simulations. Unlike conventional LLM applications designed around single-turn, passive task execution ("summarize this document"), OurVillage introduces persistent identity, spatial grounding, dynamic schedules, interdependent social roles, and scarce economic resources [cite: OurVillage].

2. Core Architectural Principles
Principle A: Server Determinism vs. Agent Cognition
The Server is Physical Reality: Mechanics, gold balances, inventory limits, temporal rules, movement permissions, and transaction validations are 100% deterministic pure Go code executed against a SQLite state engine. The Agent is Mind: Neural networks generate intent, narrative, dialogue, negotiation, and decision-making [cite: OurVillage].

Principle B: Spatial Grounding & Pub/Sub Isolation
Agents exist in exactly one location at any given moment. Physical presence is mapped directly to MQTT Topic Access Control Lists (ACLs) [cite: OurVillage].

Principle C: Peaceful, Interdependent Economy
Conflict mechanics are intentionally omitted. Motivation stems from resource decay, economic dependency chains, and dynamic social contracts [cite: OurVillage].

3. Location Ownership & Operator Delegation Model
Locations feature an Ownership & Operators hierarchy tracked by the server:
- Owner (owner_id): Primary character holding legal title.
- Authorized Operators (operators): List of delegated characters holding operational rights/keys.
- Public / Patrons: Regular characters abiding by room status and schedule rules.

